-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Jack the Nipper II - In Coconut Capers
  Publisher   Gremlin Graphics, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Jack the Nipper II - In Coconut Capers (1987)(Gremlin Graphics
              Software)[a].z80
  MD5         6f5d708c439f3356a930ea4f176a0c8f

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Every figure painted in colours of its own: Jack, the jungle's
              creatures and people, and the pickups. Only sprite colours
              change. A painted set, colourist not named.

  Changes     1.0: figures as Next sprites; Enhanced colours (every figure
              painted) as a menu choice.

  Note        Jack, the natives, the monkeys, the lion, the hippo, scorpions,
              snakes, birds and the pickups are hardware sprites, so a figure
              no longer takes the colours of the scenery it crosses; the
              scenery, the swinging rope, the panel and the text stay as the
              game draws them. It runs about 4.5% slower than the original.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite ammo
   3  Immunity

  Infinite lives and Infinite ammo are the archive's POKEs; Immunity returns
  from the death routine after it clears its counters, so a death never starts
  and a long fall lands. All checked against the code.

